.nh
.TH "BCDOCK" "1" "Jan 2025" "BCDock CLI" "BCDock Manual"

.SH NAME
bcdock-env-create - Create a new BC environment


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbcdock env create [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a new BC environment.

.PP
When --version / --country / --region are all omitted and stdin is a terminal,
the CLI fetches fast configs (versions with pre-built VM images) across all
regions and prompts you to pick one, so you only see versions that can be
created right now.

.PP
Pass the flags explicitly to skip the picker (scripts, CI, agent use).

.PP
Exit codes:
  0   ok
  1   general error, including provisioning failed or a --wait timeout
  3   auth failure (missing or invalid token)
  4   rate-limited


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--country\fP=""
	Country localisation (e.g. au, us, gb)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Skip TLS verification when publishing manifest apps to the dev endpoint

.PP
\fB--manifest\fP=""
	Path to a bcdock.manifest.yaml. Implies --wait, because apps need a running environment. Precedence: an explicitly passed flag beats the manifest, which beats the built-in default

.PP
\fB--multi-tenant\fP[=true]
	Multi-tenant mode

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Environment name

.PP
\fB--region\fP=""
	Azure region

.PP
\fB--type\fP="sandbox"
	Environment type: sandbox or onprem

.PP
\fB--version\fP=""
	BC version, full (e.g. 27.5.46862.54899); see 'bcdock artifacts list --fast-only'

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until running or failed

.PP
\fB--wait-timeout\fP=0s
	Max time to wait (default: 30m)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env: BCDOCK_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colored output

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Request timeout

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	API token (env: BCDOCK_TOKEN)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  bcdock env create
  bcdock env create --name my-env --version <version> --country au --region australiaeast --wait
    # <version>: a full version (e.g. 27.5.46862.54899) from
    # 'bcdock artifacts list --region australiaeast --fast-only'
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbcdock-env(1)\fP
